          "source": "",
          "thread": "Wormhole institutional legitimacy",
          "why": "Jump Trading spinning off Wormhole and Uniswap DAO selecting it for governance signaled to readers that crosschain infrastructure was maturing from experiment to institution."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "ERC-7683 intents standard",
          "why": "Multiple headlines about Uniswap, Across, and the Ethereum Foundation converging on a shared crosschain intents standard attracted readers tracking whether the industry would finally fragment or coalesce."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Stablecoin crosschain expansion",
          "why": "PayPal pyUSD on LayerZero and Circle USDC on Cosmos IBC showed readers that regulated stablecoin issuers were treating multichain reach as a competitive necessity."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Bridge exploit losses",
          "why": "The HTX/Heco hack and Magpie Protocol attack drew readers who wanted to track whether funds were recoverable and who bore liability."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Native Bitcoin crosschain DeFi",
          "why": "A protocol using Discreet Log Contracts to put self-custodied BTC into DeFi touched the perennial reader interest in unlocking Bitcoin's liquidity without wrapping or custody."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Chain abstraction UX paradigm",
          "why": "Products like Omni Account, Unichain, and CoW Swap's bridgeless swaps attracted readers who believe crosschain UX friction — not security — is the last barrier to mainstream DeFi adoption."
        }
      ]
    },
